Phase 3: Route Table Target Injection

Query target VPC main route tables dynamically to resolve structural dependencies, injecting reciprocal routing targets over the newly active pcx link:
bash
# 1. Fetch main Route Table reference for Public VPC
DEFAULT_RT_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-route-tables \
  --filters "Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-085ea0b72a3520fef" "Name=association.main,Values=true" \
  --query "RouteTables[0].RouteTableId" --output text --region us-east-1)

# 2. Inject Outbound Route block to target Private Subnet
aws ec2 create-route \
  --route-table-id $DEFAULT_RT_ID \
  --destination-cidr-block 10.1.0.0/16 \
  --vpc-peering-connection-id pcx-0e32e7a7ee3d44440 --region us-east-1

# 3. Fetch main Route Table reference for Private VPC
PRIVATE_RT_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-route-tables \
  --filters "Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-054a99e1a41966232" "Name=association.main,Values=true" \
  --query "RouteTables[0].RouteTableId" --output text --region us-east-1)

# 4. Inject Return Route block to target Public Subnet
aws ec2 create-route \
  --route-table-id $PRIVATE_RT_ID \
  --destination-cidr-block 172.31.0.0/16 \
  --vpc-peering-connection-id pcx-0e32e7a7ee3d44440 --region us-east-1


