Phase 4: Inbound Access & Firewall Policy Upgrades

Update Security Group entries for both target environments to clear edge connectivity paths, explicitly whitelisting SSH management boundaries and ICMP transit capabilities:
bash
# 1. Authorize local administrative public terminal IP against Public Jump Security Group
MY_IP=$(curl -s https://amazonaws.com)
PUBLIC_SG_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids $PUBLIC_INSTANCE_ID --query "Reservations[0].Instances[0].SecurityGroups[0].GroupId" --output text --region us-east-1)

aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id $PUBLIC_SG_ID \
  --protocol tcp --port 22 --cidr "${MY_IP}/32" --region us-east-1

# 2. Authorize Inbound SSH traffic from Public Subnet to Private Instance
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id $PRIVATE_SG_ID \
  --protocol tcp --port 22 --cidr 172.31.0.0/16 --region us-east-1

# 3. Authorize Inbound ICMP Echo Requests from Public Subnet across the Peering link
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id $PRIVATE_SG_ID \
  --protocol icmp --port -1 --cidr 172.31.0.0/16 --region us-east-1
Use code with caution.

Phase 5: Verification and Connectivity Testing

To execute verification, inject administrative keys using EC2 Instance Connect API boundaries to open a terminal gateway session, bypassing SSM target faults:
bash
# 1. Flash public key authorization into metadata runtimes
aws ec2-instance-connect send-ssh-public-key --instance-id $PUBLIC_INSTANCE_ID --instance-os-user ec2-user --ssh-public-key file:///root/.ssh/id_rsa.pub --region us-east-1
aws ec2-instance-connect send-ssh-public-key --instance-id $PRIVATE_INSTANCE_ID --instance-os-user ec2-user --ssh-public-key file:///root/.ssh/id_rsa.pub --region us-east-1

# 2. Inject public identity permanently into target authorized_keys configuration profile
cat /root/.ssh/id_rsa.pub | ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_rsa -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no ec2-user@98.91.244.152 "mkdir -p ~/.ssh && cat >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys && chmod 700 ~/.ssh && chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys"

# 3. Establish standard connection session to the Public Jump host
ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_rsa ec2-user@98.91.244.152


